                        


Item #:  SCP-5295

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  Access to SCP-5295 is restricted to regularly scheduled maintenance and feedings.

Cleaning and maintenance routines should be as with non-anomalous site facilities. In the event of malfunction, repair of SCP-5295 should be prioritised.

Feeding is to be carried out by supervised D-class personnel twice weekly, with approximately 5kg of meat (species irrelevant). D-class should place the food next to SCP-5295, activate, then exit the chamber promptly. If D-class has for any reason not exited the chamber within 20 seconds, the door should be locked and the next feeding may be skipped.

SCP-5295 is to be connected only to a small, isolated plumbing system, including septic tank. When the tank requires emptying, this should be done by D-class personnel no less than two days after a feeding.

Under no circumstances is any person to urinate, defecate or vomit into SCP-5295.

Description:  SCP-5295 is a faded white porcelain flush toilet estimated to date from the mid-1980s. A mostly faded stamp on the side of the cistern indicates the manufacturer to be █████. In appearance and physical composition it is unremarkable.

When SCP-5295 is used in the conventional fashion, a Type-C event may occur. Type-C events do not always occur on use, with the likelihood of an event primarily being linked to the sex of the user1 and the length of time since last feeding.

Type-C events are marked by the manifestation of the entity SCP-5295-1, an aggressive, carnivorous humanoid. Manifestation occurs within the plumbing attached to SCP-5295, generally at a distance of 5-10m from the U-bend. In a typical event, SCP-5295-1 will exit the bowl, attack the legs of its target with teeth and claws to prevent escape, then return into SCP-5295 and the attached plumbing, bringing the target with it2.

Discovery:  The Foundation was alerted to a potential anomaly by an agent embedded in law enforcement in the city of ████████, England, after a malformed human skull was discovered in a local sewage treatment plant. It was identified as belonging to Jim Hooker3, a man from a nearby village who had recently been reported missing. Foundation agents interviewed Hooker's wife, Amanda Hooker, at their home and were able to identify SCP-5295 as anomalous. It was removed and replaced with a non-anomalous model.

