Cooke:  Ah. I'm sorry.

[More footsteps, then the creaking of chairs being sat on. There is a pause, then a throat being cleared.]

Wren:  Mrs. Hooker, I'm sorry but there isn't really an easy way to say this. Yesterday evening, we recovered your husband's remains just outside ████████.

